From 162e9bf19ae1ea600528d8c21ae840adf0079908 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bf7-port <bf7@local>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 19:56:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 02/40] bf7: migrate the BF7 port onto this 4.19.325 tree

Carried over from the alps188/4.19.191 tree:
  - u_ether: flatten skbs the non-aggregating TX path cannot read (RNDIS)
  - notifier: restore the upstream double-register check
  - videolfb tag layout (lcmname at +24) and the display suspend guard
  - the TD4160 touch driver, ported from the TD4320 donor that lives here,
    wired into drivers/input/touchscreen/{Kconfig,Makefile}

Already present in this tree, so not carried: the BF7 panel, the clang-11
build fixes, and - importantly - the newer PowerVR drop with ui32DeferCount /
ui32MiscFlags and the DevmemXInt*/Devmem*2 bridges the factory userspace needs.

Two fixes this tree needed of its own:
  - scripts/mkcompile_h: clang here also prints a "Found CUDA installation"
    line, which grep ' version ' matched, putting a second line inside the
    LINUX_COMPILER string literal and breaking compile.h.
  - lsm_hook_defs.h: fs_context_parse_param declared 0 as its default return,
    but security_fs_context_parse_param() uses call_int_hook(..., -ENOPARAM, ..)
    which stops at the first non-zero.  With BPF LSM built in, every mount
    parameter was swallowed - including "source" - so fc->source stayed NULL
    and vfs_get_tree() failed every FS_REQUIRES_DEV mount with -ENOENT.  The
    root filesystem could not be mounted at all until this was corrected.
